  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 470-50, gain or loss on extinguishment equals the reacquisition price minus the carrying amount. At maturity, the carrying amount equals face value (all premium or discount is fully amortized), and the reacquisition price also equals face value. Therefore no gain or loss arises. The new bond issuance is a separate financing transaction.
Wrong (A): Future interest savings from a lower coupon rate are not recognized as a gain at the refinancing date. GAAP does not capitalize projected interest savings.
Wrong (C): The difference in coupon rates is irrelevant to the gain/loss calculation on the retired bonds; only the reacquisition price versus carrying amount matters.
Wrong (D): The $120,000 figure represents one year of interest rate difference, which is not a recognized gain under extinguishment accounting.$EXPL$
