Wrong (A): $30,000 represents a full semiannual payment (6 months of interest), not the 4-month accrual from the last payment date.
Wrong (B): $10,000 understates the accrual, reflecting only 2 months of interest rather than the correct 4-month period.
Wrong (C): $15,000 represents 3 months of interest, which would apply only if the last payment date were February 1 rather than January 1.$EXPL$
