Wrong (B): This describes a cash (sales) discount offered for early payment (e.g., 2/10, n/30), which is recorded when taken or anticipated. Trade discounts are different.
Wrong (C): A sales allowance is granted after delivery when goods are damaged or defective, not a pre-sale reduction from list price.
Wrong (D): A volume rebate is a post-purchase incentive tied to cumulative purchases, not an upfront reduction from catalog price.$EXPL$
