-- Q11973: Cash and Cash Equivalents [hard/L4]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 305-10-05 and auditing standards, a proof of cash reconciles beginning balances, receipts, disbursements, and ending balances simultaneously. When all timing differences are resolved but book receipts still exceed adjusted bank deposits, a fictitious receipt recorded on the books to conceal a cash shortage is the most likely cause.
Wrong (A): A deposit the bank failed to credit would appear as a bank-side discrepancy, not an excess of book receipts over bank deposits.
Wrong (B): An unrecorded bank service charge would reduce the adjusted book balance in the disbursements column, not inflate book receipts.
Wrong (C): An NSF check returned by the bank would appear as a bank disbursement item, not a discrepancy in the receipts column.$EXPL$
