-- Q11976: Cash and Cash Equivalents [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): A postdated check cannot be deposited or cashed until the date written on it. Because Hartwell cannot convert it to cash at December 31, it does not meet the definition of cash or cash equivalents under ASC 305-10-05. It should be classified as accounts receivable until the check date arrives and the deposit clears.
Wrong (A): Cash must be available for immediate withdrawal or use. A postdated check is not yet negotiable at the balance sheet date.
Wrong (B): Cash equivalents must have original maturities of three months or less and be readily convertible. A postdated check does not qualify under this definition.
Wrong (D): Notes receivable are formal written promises to pay with specified terms. A postdated check is an informal instrument, not a promissory note.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11976;

