Wrong (A): Offsetting against Account A is prohibited because the accounts are at different banks with no offset agreement. ASC 210-20-45 requires a legal right of setoff.
Wrong (B): Reporting the overdraft as a reduction of cash understates cash and fails to present the obligation as a liability owed to the bank.
